@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why a 595-line function's locals became a struct, and what that bought
' covers: internal/run/spec.go
' covers: internal/run/run.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/run_golden_test.go
'
' ── THE PROBLEM WAS THE STACK FRAME ────────────────────────────────────────
' doRun held SIXTY top-level locals. That is not a size complaint: it means the
' function's contract was invisible. Nothing could be moved out of it without
' first proving, by reading all 595 lines, which later line still needed the
' value — and every one of moves 2 to 5 paid that cost again.
'
' Spec is those locals, named. It is deliberately NOT a merge of the two backend
' inputs: it sits ABOVE them, and sandbox.Input / dockeregress.Input are each
' built FROM it at the seam. Merging would have made every sbx-only field (Clone,
' CPUs) legible to the docker path and every docker-only field (PidsLimit,
' ReviewSocket) legible to sbx, which is the coupling the backend split removed.
'
' ── THE ORDER OF THE TWO STEPS IS THE WHOLE TRICK ──────────────────────────
' Enumerating Spec came FIRST, as a change that altered nothing else: the struct
' was declared, filled where each local settled, and the consumers switched to
' read it. Only then was the body sliced. Slicing first would have meant
' discovering the contract and changing the structure in one diff, with no step
' where a green suite meant anything.
'
' ── WHERE THIS DEPARTS FROM THE PLAN, AND WHY ──────────────────────────────
' The plan names seven stages:
'   resolveWorkspace · resolveCredentials · promptChoices · buildPosture ·
'   selectBackend · execute · teardown
' The shipped set differs in two ways, both forced by output ORDER:
'   * promptChoices runs BEFORE resolveCredentials, not after. The prompt needs
'     the env-file lookup, and the auth report needs the answers, so the real
'     order is workspace -> lookup -> prompt -> auth.
'   * assembleEnv is a stage of its own. The plan folds it into
'     resolveCredentials, but posture is rendered BETWEEN the two; moving either
'     across that line changes the order the operator reads them in.
'   * teardown is not a stage. It is `defer` inside execute, so a signal
'     mid-run unwinds exactly the way a normal exit does.
' Stages are contiguous slices of the original statement order. Nothing was
' reordered, because reordering is precisely what the golden below forbids.
'
' ── THE PROOF HAD A HOLE, AND IT WAS THIS MOVE'S HOLE ───────────────────────
' Moves 2 to 5 were proved by the plan goldens. Those call dockeregress.Assemble
' and sandbox.Spec DIRECTLY: they pin the backends and say nothing about the
' resolve path that feeds them — which is the only thing this move touches. The
' resolve path's sole coverage was the e2e ladder, which is slow and skips
' without credentials.
' cmd/proveo/run_golden_test.go closes that hole: it drives a whole `--print` run
' under a pinned environment and pins the bytes, ui narrative included. It was
' written and captured BEFORE the split, so its passing afterwards is evidence
' rather than decoration.
title internal/run — the contract that was a stack frame

participant "cmd/proveo\nwiring" as CMD <<app>>
participant "run.Do" as DO <<app>>
participant "Spec\nthe resolved contract" as SPEC <<data>>
participant "sandbox.Input" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "dockeregress.Input" as DOC <<cloud>>

CMD ARROW_MAIN DO : Params (flags) + Deps (terminal, gh, docker)
DO ARROW_MAIN SPEC : resolveWorkspace · promptChoices · resolveCredentials
DO ARROW_MAIN SPEC : buildPosture · assembleEnv
SPEC ARROW_QUEUE SBX : selectBackend, when sbx is ready
SPEC ARROW_QUEUE DOC : execute, otherwise

note over CMD
  **Deps is what keeps this package honest.** Every
  terminal prompt, the gh session and the image
  pulls stay in ""cmd/proveo"" and arrive as
  functions: ""ManifestFor"", ""PickProject"",
  ""PromptEnv"", ""GitHubTokenEnv"",
  ""ProvisionConfirm"", ""PreflightImages"".

  ""SquidConfig"" rides along for a different
  reason — the ROOT package embeds it, and
  ""internal/"" reaching back up for it breaks the
  sidecar images, which copy only ""cmd/"" and
  ""internal/"". ""TestInternalPackagesDoNotImportRoot""
  caught exactly that, left behind by move 5.
end note

note over SPEC
  **Sixty locals, named once.** ""sid"", ""egDir"",
  ""uid""/""gid"", ""mounts"", ""workdir"", ""lookup"",
  ""detected"", ""homePlan"" — the values the plan
  called doRun's hidden contract.

  The conversion was done with ""gofmt -r"", not
  with a regex. A text pass had already rewritten
  ""\"-browser\""" to ""\"-rs.Browser\""" inside a string
  literal; an AST rewrite cannot reach into
  strings or comments, which is the only reason
  that class of damage was caught rather than
  shipped.
end note
@enduml
